As the committal hearing continued, a full summary of all the available evidence implicating Ivan Millat was detailed. When the backpack belonging to Simone Schmiddle was presented with the initials I am written on the inside flap, Ivan yelled from across the room, accusing the police of writing the initials themselves. This assertion was contradicted when Ivan's sister-in-law Joan testified that the initials were already on the backpack when he gave it to her in late 1992. Over 200 witnesses were called before the court, including Steve Wright, the British
